rockchip: recognize the RK3506 SARADC when checking the download key

The Lyra Ultra device tree names its SARADC node adc@ff4e8000. The
generic download-key check only looks for devices named saradc*, so it
never samples the key on ADC channel 1. Accept the RK3506 compatible
string as well, retaining the existing lookup for older device trees.

Keep this patch in the Lyra Ultra board directory. The existing download
path sets BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD and resets into BootROM download mode; it
does not start the vendor U-Boot's Loader-mode gadget.

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -51,7 +51,8 @@ __weak int rockchip_dnl_key_pressed(void)
 
 	ret = -ENODEV;
 	uclass_foreach_dev(dev, uc) {
-		if (!strncmp(dev->name, "saradc", 6)) {
+		if (!strncmp(dev->name, "saradc", 6) ||
+		    device_is_compatible(dev, "rockchip,rk3506-saradc")) {
 			ret = adc_channel_single_shot(dev->name, 1, &val);
 			break;
 		}
